# Alignment Record

**Request:** Add export-to-CSV to the dashboard table view.
**Target user:** Internal analysts and ops leads using the dashboard.

## Primary workflow & success condition
- Toolbar "Export CSV" button → immediate browser download of the currently visible table (same filters, sort, columns) → file `dashboard-table-YYYYMMDD.csv` (local date), openable in Excel without mangled characters.

## Decisions and assumptions
- `DECIDED` — No modal, no options, no email/queue. Scope = current view only.
- `DECIDED` — Source of truth = same query/data layer rendering the table; no persistence, retention, or migration; soft-deleted rows excluded.
- `DECIDED` — Client-side CSV generation (vetted serializer) + Blob download; no new API, timeouts, or retries.
- `DECIDED` — Permissions mirror existing table-view permission; PII columns exported only to already-authorized viewers.
- `DECIDED` — Local date in filename; desktop-only (mobile out of scope).
- `ASSUMED` — Date in filename is local, not UTC (user confirmed, so upgraded to DECIDED).

## Edge-case behavior
- Empty table → headers-only CSV + toast "No rows to export".
- >5,000 rows → confirmation dialog before export.
- Failure → error toast, no partial file.
- Escaping/encoding: standard CSV quoting, UTF-8, verified round-trip in Excel.

## Security / integrations / data
- No new role, no export audit log in v1 (HITL flagged).
- No external service dependency.
- `RESEARCH` (deferred spike) — "export all matching rows" beyond loaded rows for server-paginated tables: question = endpoint shape; budget ≤1 day; evidence = required API contract; unblocks only if stakeholders demand it.

## Explicit non-goals
- Scheduled/server-side exports, PDF/Excel formats, custom column mapping, CSV import/re-import, export history UI, cross-table exports, mobile layout, export auditing (pending HITL).

## Testing & acceptance
- Unit tests: CSV serializer (quoting, escaping, UTF-8, empty). Component test: button enabled/disabled and filename. One E2E: happy-path download. Manual QA: Excel, LibreOffice, Google Sheets.

## Unresolved risks & owners
- `HITL` — Export auditing requirement → compliance/security review if requested.
- `RESEARCH` — Server-paginated "export all" → bounded spike, owner = feature team, only when demanded.
- Reversible: client-only change; feature flag optional if rollback requested.

**Stop conditions met:** all applicable areas decided/marked; workflow and success condition concrete; non-goals and risky boundaries recorded; unresolved items assigned to HITL/RESEARCH. Material items: no outstanding `ASSUMED` items — every line is DECIDED, HITL, or RESEARCH.

